<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arikesari II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arikesari II was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vemulawada">Vemulavada</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, feudatories of the Rashtrakutas. He is remembered as the patron of the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adikavi-pampa">Pampa</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> epics <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramarjuna-vijaya">Vikramarjuna Vijaya</a> and Adipurana were written at his court around 941 and celebrate him through the figure of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arjuna">Arjuna</a>.</p></div>
